<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|article>

<\body>
  <section|Format text and navigate>

  Formatting is part of the document tree. Select content, then apply a text
  style or insert a mathematical structure around the caret.

  <subsection|Try the formatting tools>

  Select the words <strong|bold example> and choose Format, then Text, then
  Bold. Select the words <em|italic example> and choose Italic. The visible
  style remains attached to the selected text as you keep editing.

  In a formula, try a superscript and subscript:

  <\equation*>
    x<rsup|2> + a<rsub|n>
  </equation*>

  <subsection|Keyboard shortcuts>

  Press F2 while the editor has focus to open Tessera's shortcut layer. Type
  the shown key for an action, such as F for a fraction or S for a section.
  Press 0 to enter a native TeXmacs key sequence, choose modifiers with 1 to
  4, press Enter, then type the final key.

  Escape cancels a shortcut sequence. The toolbar and Find a tool search are
  available when you prefer to choose a command by name.

  <strong|Practice:> select a sentence in this lesson, make it bold, then
  undo and redo the change. Insert a fraction inside the displayed equation
  and move into its numerator with the arrow keys.
</body>
